{{!
    @template local_moodesk/composer_attachment_list

    The files waiting in the reply composer's draft area, one row each.

    Rendered by amd/src/composer_attachments.js from what the server reports the
    draft holds — never from what was just clicked, so a failed upload or a
    refused delete leaves the list telling the truth. With an empty draft this
    template is not rendered at all.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * files - array of files in the draft
      * filename      - name as stored
      * filepath      - path within the draft area, normally '/'
      * sizeformatted - human-readable size
      * url           - draft file URL, for checking a file before sending

    Example context (json):
    {
        "files": [
            {
                "filename": "screenshot.png",
                "filepath": "/",
                "sizeformatted": "241.2KB",
                "url": "https://example.com/draftfile.php/5/user/draft/1/screenshot.png"
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<ul class="mhd-composer__files">
  {{#files}}
  <li class="mhd-composer__file">
    <svg class="mhd-composer__file-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <use href="#mhd-icon-file"></use>
    </svg>
    <a href="{{url}}" class="mhd-composer__file-name" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"
       title="{{filename}}">{{filename}}</a>
    <span class="mhd-composer__file-size">{{sizeformatted}}</span>
    <button type="button" class="mhd-composer__file-remove"
            data-action="mhd-remove-attachment"
            data-filename="{{filename}}"
            data-filepath="{{filepath}}"
            aria-label="{{#str}} attachment_remove, local_moodesk, {{filename}} {{/str}}">
      <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
    </button>
  </li>
  {{/files}}
</ul>
